 {"id": "TJ-DF-039", "type": null, "priority": "P2", "status": "complete", "title": "[P2] PyYAML-less fresh host: user rules mirror fails open silently and rules-drift-probe reports drift=0 exit 0 on an unparseable mirror", "description": null, "acceptance_criteria": null, "created_at": "2026-09-28T23:01:14+00:00", "created_by": null, "worker_status": "pending", "foreman_note": null, "reasoning": "Fresh Debian bunker agent (no python3-yaml, PEP 668 blocks pip), HEAD 14a6f46: the engine reads ~/.config/terminal-jail/rules.d/00-builtins.yaml via PyYAML; without it the mirror is unparseable and fails open - built-ins keep working but any user-authored rule in the mirror never loads, with no verdict-time message. scripts/rules-drift-probe.py prints exactly one line 'WARNING: unparseable rule file (engine fails open)' and then 'RESULT: drift=0', exit 0 - the tool whose job is catching a stale/broken mirror calls the broken mirror clean. The install-time pack skip is honest now (TJ-DF-024/025 fixed, verified live this run); the gap is only the runtime mirror path and the probe exit policy. Fix direction: --fail-on-drift classifies an unparseable mirror as a drift-class condition with a named remediation (install the distro python3-yaml package), or the wrapper warns once at verdict time when the mirror cannot be parsed. Evidence: docs/dogfood/2026-09-28-fresh-install-smoke.md; repro on bunker-las-03 agent 875dedf2 (destroyed).", "complexity": 3, "updated_at": "2026-09-28T23:01:14+00:00", "detail": {"fingerprint": "2746f9ac9983031d7ad56b5c7c7a13b98b2116e3e739165810218f4443404561"}, "commit_hash": "bee7b65", "worker_summary": "rules.py JSON-fallback now emits a loud stderr note naming file+cause on PyYAML-less parse failure (parse_notes, fail-open action unchanged); rules-drift-probe counts corrupt mirror files as first-class (RESULT carries corrupt=N, --fail-on-drift exits 1 on drift or corrupt, bare run still 0). 10 tests added, RED proven on reverted tree. Full suite 150